{"c":[{"id":"43e4c498eba10341","sum":"A12: debug-socket 'inject helperLine' takes the helper route, gate included (pass your own --settings). SurfaceGate forgives Grammarly's layer-1 ring (field +64 pt) via the live focused frame, or every TextEdit offer is held covered.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T155327Z-d8b7c9de6967162d","text":"Debug-socket 'inject helperLine' takes the helper-socket route, gate included (A12): an injected action is a helper offer whose Tab sends offerAccept. Scripts that inject must pass their own --settings, or a paused or Fill-off user file refuses it.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T182128Z-e49f48ead18a928c","text":"Grammarly Desktop (UIElement agent) keeps a layer-1 alpha-1 window at the focused field grown 64 pt per side; SurfaceGate skips such agent rings via the live focused frame (ringsField), or every TextEdit offer is held 'covered' (A12).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"beeb162738aa9a6a","sum":"GUI runs: background-exec'd TextEdit never fronts (open -b only when ours is sole TextEdit, then Bring All to Front); own HID keys reset HIDIdleTime (A12). Event cards judge only the last finished sentence, arriving as a change from an empty body (B17).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T182135Z-3ee5b6c917cf77a7","text":"Desktop GUI runs: TextEdit exec'd from the background never takes the front; open -b com.apple.TextEdit (only when ours is the sole TextEdit) plus its Window > Bring All to Front does. Our own HID keys reset HIDIdleTime, so gate the next leg on no input since the last (A12).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T191104Z-3aee21889eca1d38","text":"Event cards judge only the last finished sentence of what is typed: a test body must end with the event sentence and arrive as a change (empty body first), or no attend question is asked (B17 privacy session).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
